WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.701
-I don't know -- I don't know
how you do it.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.367
But you just wrapped
"Better Call Saul"

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.367
and you already filmed
a whole new other series.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.133
-Whoa! One series?

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.934
I actually -- Two.

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.300
-What? I didn't --
-You know, there's anot--

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.801
-I didn't know you had
another show.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.834
-Well, yeah.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:18.434
This -- I joined the cast of
"Blippi" this season.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:20.868
-The -- The children's show,
"Blippi"?

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:22.834
-Did you write that?
-No.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:26.501
-Well, I play Blippi's
evil nemesis, Gorpi.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.267
-I didn't even know
Blippi had a nemesis.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:33.100
I mean, what's going
on the show?

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.767
-Just a lot of Blippi stuff,
you know.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.567
I mean, basically -- I guess
I should say spoiler alert.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:45.267
But my character, Gorpi, stole
Blippi's magic strawberry

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.133
that teaches him the alphabet.
-Wow.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:50.033
-And now Blippi can't speak
because he forgot the alphabet.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:54.734
So that means he can't RSVP to
Mr. Toothbrush's cleanup party.

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:57.634
But what Blippi doesn't know,
right,

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:00.167
is that I've kidnapped his date
to the cleanup party,

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.634
Mavis Manners.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.133
And this is throwing the
entire world into turmoil

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.801
because now -- and you guys --
you already know this.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.934
But anyway, no one knows how to
say "please and thank you."

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:12.367
Also, just this entire season is

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:14.200
a dream that the number eight
is having.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.334
-Well, this is --
It's interesting.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:20.100
I wouldn't think that you would
do a children's show.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.634
-Well, I mean, they paid me
a lot of money.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.467
Plus, they gave me complete
creative control.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:30.167
You know what? They even let me
write my own dialogue.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.334
I brought a clip if you guys
want to --

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:35.767
-Can we do that?
-Let's go.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.000
Can we see it?
-Rick, can we see it?

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.868
-Can we see it?
Is there any way to see it?

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:42.100
Do you have any TVs?
-Bob Odenkirk as the villain

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.234
Gorpi in the new season of
"Blippi."

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.634
-It's happening.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.234
-♪ So much to learn about ♪

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.801
♪ It'll make you want to shout ♪

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.901
-♪ Blippi ♪

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:54.267
-Alright, listen up,
you pieces of [bleep].

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:57.334
Basically, [bleep]!

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.200
Blippi just met a talking crayon

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.601
that taught him how to tie
his [bleep] shoes.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:03.801
You're the only three letters
I trust.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.901
A, Q, Z.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.334
Here's what we're going to do.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:12.067
A, I want you to break into
Professor Naptime's treehouse.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:14.167
Steal that [bleep]
finger paints.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.367
Z, I need you to put down
the apple slices and [bleep] up

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.434
Barry Broccoli at lunchtime

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.100
when he's singing
his healthy lunch song.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.367
Make it look like an "accident."

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:27.567
And, Q, I need to you find out
when Blippi is taking his

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.801
next bubble bath because I'm
going to teach

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:34.267
that mother[bleep] a little
something about electricity.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.133
[ Laughs maniacally ]

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.167
-Blippi!

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.200
-Wow!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.234
Wow, Bob Odenkirk --
-I've just been working.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:44.968
I've just been working.
-Yeah, I'm so happy.

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.734
Congratulations. Bob Odenkirk.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:51.000
"Lucky Hank" premieres
this Sunday on AMC and AMC+.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.801
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

